From: Peter Jeremy <peter.jeremy () auss2 ! alcatel ! com ! au>
Date: Sun, 28 Feb 1999 21:37:10 +0000
To: freebsd-alpha
Subject: Improving bcmp et al
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=freebsd-alpha&m=103030573206969

I notice that FreeBSD/Alpha still uses the standard (portable) bcmp()
implementation in libkern.  Combined with gcc-2.7.2, this gives very
poor performance.  

I recently wrote a somewhat improved bcmp() that provides a substantial
speed-up: 3-5 times with gcc2.7.2, twice as fast again with DEC's cc.
Further details are in my post to -hackers on Thu Feb 25 10:35:36 1999 +1100

Peter


