> FreeBSD -P www.freebsd.org -A FreeBSD_3_1_Alpha -V FBSD31 [dir]

I'm not exactly sure how SRM wants a bootable CD arranged but I suspect
that its the same as a bootable disk - the bootstrap needs to be in a
contiguous region and the first disk block has two fields with the block
address and size of the bootstrap.

I think NetBSD has some code for making bootable cds for alphas but I
don't have the source tree handy right now...

